osts’ certificates for the wallet’s own HTTPS requests:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"host → base64 SHA-256 digests of a certificate’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SubjectPublicKeyInfo, one of which a certificate in the verified","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"chain must have, or the request fails as ","type":"text"},{"code":"tlsPin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" before anything","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is sent. A host is a name, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"*.","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and one, matching any name a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"label below it; not an IP address. Pins add to certificate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"verification, never replace it: pin a CA’s key, so a leaf renewal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t break the app, and keep a backup pin. They cover the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests the SDK makes (issuers, Authorization Servers,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Verifiers, status lists), not the app’s own, such as to its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Wallet Provider: pin that client yourself.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/oid4vcwallet\/walletconfiguration\/network-swift.struct\/tlspins","role":"symbol"},"doc://oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet/documentation/OID4VCWallet":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/oid4vcwallet","role":"collection","title":"OID4VCWallet","abstract":[{"text":"Receive verifiable credentials and present them from an iOS app: over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"OpenID4VCI and OpenID4VP under HAIP, to Safari’s Digital Credentials","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API, and in person over Bluetooth.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet"},"doc://oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet/documentation/OID4VCWallet/WalletConfiguration/Network-swift.struct/allowedPrivateHosts":{"title":"allowedPrivateHosts","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/oid4vcwallet.OID4VCWallet\/documentation\/OID4VCWallet\/WalletConfiguration\/Network-swift.struct\/allowedPrivateHosts","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"allowedPrivateHosts","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Hosts the wallet may reach at a private address (10\/8, 172.16\/12,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"192.168\/16, fc00::\/7) outside ","type":"text"},{"code":"development","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": issuers, Verifiers,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"status lists and CRL distribution points inside the deployment’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own network, an enterprise’s or a test environment’s. Each is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"host name, matched exactly and without case: no wildcard, IP","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"address, port or loopback name. Nothing else is lifted: a listed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"host is still refused at a loopback or link-local address, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every request is still HTTPS with its certificate verified. List","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only hosts the deployment runs: anyone who can hand the wallet an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"offer or a request can have it send a request to them.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/oid4vcwallet\/walletconfiguration\/network-swift.s